# What Vercel uploads. The deployment unit is the repository, not web/, because
# the interface imports the hook's arithmetic from ts/src/simulate.ts — the one
# file a differential test checks against Solidity. A copy inside web/ would
# drift, so the build has to be able to see the original.
#
# Everything below is either a build artifact, a dependency tree Vercel installs
# itself, or Foundry material that has no part in rendering a page.

node_modules
**/node_modules

# Foundry: dependencies, compiler output, and the cache that indexes it.
lib
out
cache
forge-cache
broadcast

# Solidity and its tests. Deployed and immutable; the site reads them from the
# chain, never from disk.
src
test
script
foundry.toml
foundry.lock
remappings.txt

# Explorer submission bundles and deployment records — the site reads addresses
# from lib/chain.ts, not from these.
verification
deployments
docs
quench-redesign-prompt.md

# The simulator's own tests and build output; only ts/src is imported.
ts/dist
ts/test

# Next's local build directories.
web/.next
web/.next-build
web/shots
